A policy on `zm-1.10.2-r1`, zenoh-modem's zenoh fork, narrows every other
principal over the fork's link protocols (`link.v2` §2.4), so its subjects
name `unixsock-dgram`, which stock zenoh 1.10.1's loader refuses (#1044).
The router config is then read as data, in zenoh's shapes and the
binding's link protocols, and the note says so. zenoh-modem's RF router,
running the block `acl gen` wrote, and the ground's client running the
block `acl gen --far-config` wrote, the catalog the ground holds beside
them: exit 0.

